  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> be solutions of the differential equations <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>dx</mi><mi>dt</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>ax</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>dy</mi><mi>dt</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>by</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> respectively, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>. Given that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mo>;</mo><mo> </mo><mi>y</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><mi>y</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi>x</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>, for which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msub><mn>2</mn></math>",
